WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:05.750
The defeat of a self-proclaimed god, the imminent
death of the Warrior Nun, and an approaching

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:06.750
holy war.

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:10.849
The ending of "Warrior Nun" Season 2 is filled
with unexpected revelations.

00:00:11.663 --> 00:00:14.780
Sleazy demon Adriel is the big bad of Season
2.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:17.410
And he makes for an incredibly vivid villain.

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:21.810
His syrupy tone is perfectly emblematic of
his charming, manipulative, and fundamentally

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:23.510
deceitful ways.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:27.840
Adriel is a thief who steals the Halo from
Reya, a being who rules the realm on the other

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.119
side of the portal.

00:00:29.119 --> 00:00:33.230
Disguising himself as a human, he's well on
his way to establishing his own powerful cult

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:36.930
when the first Warrior Nun, Areala, skillfully
tricks him.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:40.120
He is subsequently entombed for a thousand
years.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:45.460
When he's freed by Ava and the Order, he immediately
becomes the leader of a brand new cult.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:50.786
Adriel is the one responsible for encouraging
Dr. Jillian Salvius to create a dimensional portal.

00:00:50.786 --> 00:00:56.050
He lures her top assistant Kristian into his
cult, and uses technology from ARQ-Tech to

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:59.350
focus the prayers of his followers, making
him invincible.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:04.629
He proceeds to use that tech to perform apparent
miracles, like healing boils, stopping a plague

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:08.020
of locusts, and dispelling a fear-causing
fog.

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:12.920
Of course, he's also the source of these ills,
which he creates using his cutting-edge gadgets.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:16.939
Just when it seems like he's powerful enough
to trap Reya and kill Ava, the Warrior Nun

00:01:16.939 --> 00:01:19.940
summons the monstrous Tarasks from the Other
Side.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:21.909
They tear him limb from limb.

00:01:21.909 --> 00:01:23.360
It's a perfect end.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:27.070
Adriel brags that nothing in the human realm
can kill him, so Ava simply brings over the

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:28.689
thing he's been fleeing.

00:01:28.689 --> 00:01:32.960
It remains to be seen if he'll actually stay
dead, but it's obvious that his death unclouds

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.764
the minds of his followers.

00:01:35.713 --> 00:01:39.072
Throughout Season 2, Ava is in training to
defeat Adriel.

00:01:39.072 --> 00:01:43.690
While she gains more control over her powers,
which include energy blasts and the ability

00:01:43.690 --> 00:01:47.219
to phase through objects, they suddenly fail
her at random times.

00:01:47.219 --> 00:01:48.590
"The Halo just sort of gave out.

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:53.380
It's not like it was running out of power,
it's just like someone flipped off a switch."

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:58.180
This is all thanks to Adriel's gigantic cross,
which acts as a siphon for mystical energy,

00:01:58.180 --> 00:01:59.180
even prayers.

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:04.170
The uncertainty and rebelliousness Ava demonstrates
in Season 1 are gone, as her sisters in the

00:02:04.170 --> 00:02:06.710
Order of the Cruciform Sword become her priority.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.690
She accepts them, and they accept her.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:13.680
Ava resigns herself to the idea of having
to sacrifice her own life to defeat Adriel.

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:17.770
Miguel, who has returned from the Other Side
to kill Adriel, tells Ava that he's a bomb

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.849
and she's the fuse that will set him off.

00:02:19.849 --> 00:02:23.980
Ava manages to survive that eventual detonation,
but she's mortally wounded in her fight with

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:25.830
Adriel and Lilith.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:29.881
After Adriel's destruction, she's content
to die and give the Halo to Beatrice, but

00:02:29.881 --> 00:02:33.300
Lilith suggests putting her through the gate
to the Other Side.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:36.319
No one knows how this will affect her, but
it will save her life.

00:02:36.319 --> 00:02:40.819
Miguel and Lilith both came back from the
Other Side and were greatly changed, but neither

00:02:40.819 --> 00:02:42.270
carried the Halo.

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:44.379
What will Ava be like when she returns?

00:02:44.379 --> 00:02:45.620
We don't yet know.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:51.720
No character on "Warrior Nun" has enjoyed
crazier swerves than Sister Lilith.

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:55.650
Her main ambition in Season 1 is to be the
one who receives the Halo after Sister Shannon

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:56.680
is killed.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:00.490
When Ava gets it instead, she's furious and
sets out on a mission to kill her.

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:04.760
But instead, a monstrous Tarask kills her
while she hunts down Ava.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:09.124
Surprisingly, Lilith not only returns from
the dead but comes back with terrifying new powers.

00:03:09.124 --> 00:03:13.769
Her demonic claws and quantum teleportation
make her a powerful ally for the Order when

00:03:13.769 --> 00:03:14.801
she returns.

00:03:14.801 --> 00:03:20.220
However, Lilith finds her skin becoming scaly
in Season 2 and turns to Dr. Jillian Salvius

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.220
for help.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:25.129
Jillian examines the scales and suspects a
mutation of some kind, but is unable to provide

00:03:25.129 --> 00:03:26.930
her with any real answers.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:31.100
When Lilith goes to Adriel, the slippery manipulator
unlocks her potential.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:35.809
This includes giving her sight that allows
her to see demons, as well as huge, bat-like wings.

00:03:35.809 --> 00:03:37.729
In other words, she's a demon nun.

00:03:37.813 --> 00:03:41.510
Adriel's sweet-talking preys on Lilith's jealousy
of Ava.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:46.090
Moreover, there's a kernel of truth in Adriel's
arguments about seeking freedom from a capricious

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:48.190
God who doesn't answer prayers.

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:50.870
He uses this to manipulate her with dreadful
skill.

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:53.730
In time, she becomes more than a match for
the Warrior Nun.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:58.720
In the end, Lilith sees Adriel as the monster
he truly is and develops her own agenda.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:03.220
Thus, she warns Beatrice that a holy war is
coming, and hopes they're on the same side.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:08.790
The betrayal of Father Vincent at the end
of Season 1 is a truly wild moment.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:13.390
His story as a former hitman and alcoholic
who redeems himself in the priesthood is touching

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:16.329
until it's revealed that he's Adriel's biggest
accomplice.

00:04:16.329 --> 00:04:20.480
He betrays the trust of everyone in the Order
of the Cruciform Sword and continues to act

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:23.310
as Adriel's right-hand man in Season 2.

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:27.914
Vincent buys into Adriel's rhetoric about
freedom and fighting the oppression of the church.

00:04:27.914 --> 00:04:32.033
However, the more that Adriel grandstands,
the more Vincent starts to have doubts.

00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:34.560
This comes to a head when Adriel kills the
Pope.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:38.970
Father Vincent grabs the Crown of Thorns,
which can render supernatural beings powerless,

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:41.600
and gives it to Ava instead of returning it
to Adriel.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:43.970
Ava sees his doubts and approaches him.

00:04:43.970 --> 00:04:47.310
Mother Superion spares Vincent's life earlier
in the season.

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:51.410
This act of mercy winds up helping everyone,
as Father Vincent aids the Order in the final

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:52.830
battle against Adriel.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:56.789
Where the disillusioned priest will go next
is unclear, especially since he takes off

00:04:56.789 --> 00:04:58.461
his collar in the finale.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:04.539
One of the central plots of Season 1 is Dr.
Jillian Salvius' attempts to save the life

00:05:04.539 --> 00:05:07.169
of her son, Michael, who has a rare blood
disease.

00:05:07.169 --> 00:05:12.820
Notably, Michael has visions of Adriel's tomb,
the Warrior Nun, and other supernatural phenomena.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:17.110
Jillian creates a mystical gate to send him
to a heaven-like place where he can be healthy.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:20.910
When she finally makes the gate work, young
Michael runs through it and disappears.

00:05:20.910 --> 00:05:23.320
Jillian has no idea how to get him back.

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:27.889
At the beginning of Season 2, Ava befriends
a young man named Miguel, who opposes Adriel.

00:05:27.889 --> 00:05:30.630
He soon invites Ava to help him and his organization.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:34.330
Very quickly, Ava learns there's much more
to Miguel than meets the eye.

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:38.610
This becomes especially obvious when he helps
her defeat several demon-possessed people.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:42.319
When he tells them they're going to go to
his home, which is a safe place for them to

00:05:42.319 --> 00:05:44.590
stay, they find themselves at Jillian's house.

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:47.300
It's here that Miguel reveals that he's her
son.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:51.211
The tragedy of the situation is that while
Jillian is overjoyed to see him alive, she's

00:05:51.211 --> 00:05:54.030
also still in mourning about the time she
lost with him.

00:05:54.030 --> 00:05:57.920
Unbeknownst to her, his situation is even
more tragic than it appears to be.

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:01.540
His only purpose in returning is to carry
out a suicide mission.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:05.650
Once again, a character who tries to play
God, Jillian in this case, is punished for

00:06:05.650 --> 00:06:06.819
her hubris.

00:06:07.781 --> 00:06:11.990
One of the most slow-burn character developments
in "Warrior Nun" is the friendship that eventually

00:06:11.990 --> 00:06:15.289
turns into love between Ava and Sister Beatrice.

00:06:15.289 --> 00:06:19.699
Beatrice struggles with feelings of worthlessness
and fears of rejection because she is a lesbian.

00:06:19.699 --> 00:06:23.270
She responds to these thorny emotions with
obsessive overachieving.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:27.350
When Beatrice tells a story about a Warrior
Nun who was gay, Ava immediately understands

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:30.330
that this is Beatrice's way of coming out
to her.

00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:34.270
Their friendship deepens in Season 2, as they
both take jobs at a local bar in Switzerland

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:36.410
in an attempt to lay low.

00:06:36.410 --> 00:06:39.949
Beatrice is trying to train Ava, but Ava has
her eye on having fun.

00:06:39.949 --> 00:06:44.479
When Beatrice tells Ava that she's never had
a drink, Ava is determined to get her drunk.

00:06:44.479 --> 00:06:47.259
They have a great time and dance with each
other at a bar.

00:06:47.259 --> 00:06:51.639
Their budding love comes into sharper focus
when it appears that Ava is dead from a fall.

00:06:51.639 --> 00:06:55.190
Before Ava revives, Beatrice cradles her and
pours out her heart.

00:06:55.190 --> 00:07:00.459
As the season continues, Ava knows that their
time together is limited and kisses a shocked Beatrice.

00:07:00.459 --> 00:07:04.699
Before sending Ava to the Other Side, they
have another tender moment, but Beatrice doesn't

00:07:04.699 --> 00:07:07.401
tell Ava she loves her until after she crosses
over.

00:07:07.401 --> 00:07:12.288
"I love you."

00:07:12.413 --> 00:07:16.580
It's clear that this will be something that
propels the action as the series moves forward,

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:22.282
as their love story is an excellent anchor
amidst all the weirdness of "Warrior Nun."

00:07:22.282 --> 00:07:25.080
Mother Superion has her own journey in Season
2.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:29.759
She's a stodgy enforcer in Season 1, disapproving
of everything that Ava does, and works closely

00:07:29.759 --> 00:07:33.410
with Cardinal Duretti to keep the Order of
the Cruciform Sword viable.

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:38.069
However, she comes around and helps the sisters
invade the Vatican at the end of Season 1.

00:07:38.069 --> 00:07:41.050
Season 2 sees her truly come to grips with
her past.

00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:44.610
She reveals the full story of how she held
and was rejected by the Halo.

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:48.830
While on a mission, her insistence on working
alone wound up getting the previous Mother

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:49.830
Superion killed.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:54.550
Her arrogance made the Halo drop out of her
body, and Sister Shannon became her replacement.

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:57.830
This makes her resentful of Shannon and even
more resentful of Ava.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:02.490
Later, when Superion is gunned down, she confesses
her jealousy to Ava and the others.

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:04.650
Ava forgives her and lies down with her.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:09.110
Ava's unconscious use of the Halo to heal
brings Superion back to life and makes her

00:08:09.110 --> 00:08:11.319
feel healthier than she has in years.

00:08:11.319 --> 00:08:14.849
She also feels closer to the sisters than
ever before, having finally admitted to her

00:08:14.849 --> 00:08:17.412
festering feelings and personal flaws.

00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:22.790
One of the most entertaining relationships
in "Warrior Nun" is between Sister Yasmine

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:24.259
and Sister Camila.

00:08:24.259 --> 00:08:28.289
Both of them start Season 2 as secondary characters
who need to prove themselves and eventually

00:08:28.289 --> 00:08:31.440
emerge as legitimate butt-kickers in their
own ways.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:35.310
Camila is the youngest member of the Order
of the Cruciform Sword, but she's a brilliant

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:39.229
woman whose understanding of technology makes
her a crucial team member.

00:08:39.229 --> 00:08:43.110
Even when Adriel implants her with a device
that allows him to read her thoughts and speak

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:47.140
to her, Camila manages to turn the tables
on him by getting in his head at just the

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:48.230
right time.

00:08:48.230 --> 00:08:52.790
Yasmine is part of an order dedicated to protecting
the Crown of Thorns, the weapon that temporarily

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:56.510
deprogrammed Adriel and allowed Areala to
imprison him.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:09:00.990
When Adriel is let loose upon the world, Yasmine
tracks down the Order to inform the Warrior

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:02.520
Nun about the Crown's existence.

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:06.680
While guiding them to the Crown in a museum
heist, Yasmine quickly has to figure out how

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:09.600
to navigate the violent and dangerous world
of the Order.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:13.330
Yasmine and Camila are key players in the
final battle against Adriel.

00:09:13.330 --> 00:09:16.940
Camila takes out a whole gang of thugs, while
Yasmine manages to stab one of the leaders

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:18.250
who bleeds out.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:21.359
Both will likely have even more significant
roles in the future.

00:09:22.134 --> 00:09:25.780
There are times when it's hard to tell the
difference between the heroes and villains

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:26.820
of "Warrior Nun."

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:31.180
This is especially true of authority figures,
and the show's Pope is no exception.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:35.790
In Season 1, he's Cardinal Francesco Duretti,
a man obsessed with appearances, who clamps

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:39.510
down on the activities of the Order of the
Cruciform Sword because he doesn't want them

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:41.320
making the church look bad.

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:45.100
But his manipulations and schemes make it
a little too easy for the order to suspect

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:49.769
that he killed Sister Shannon and tried to
get Adriel's bones to consolidate power.

00:09:49.769 --> 00:09:51.480
This suspicion turns out to be wrong.

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:56.157
However, just because he didn't do those things
doesn't mean he's not a power-hungry and ruthless man.

00:09:56.157 --> 00:10:01.660
He tortures one of Adriel's spies to get information,
grandstands at a meeting of clergy to browbeat

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:06.570
them into working against Adriel, and is part
of an institution that has, Adriel asserts,

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:08.680
killed millions of people throughout its history.

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:12.630
The Pope is fighting against Adriel not because
it's a righteous cause, but because he's worried

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:14.437
about someone stepping on his turf.

00:10:14.437 --> 00:10:18.470
"Next to Adriel, you are as ants.

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:20.889
You will kneel before him."

00:10:20.889 --> 00:10:25.140
If there's a God on Earth, then what use will
people have for the church?

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:29.680
Adriel is presented as a charlatan, but he
cleverly co-opts all of the church's rhetoric.

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:34.120
When Duretti gets disintegrated by Adriel
on live television, it's a declaration and

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:35.480
demonstration of power.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.573
It's horrifying, yet it confirms Adriel's
claims.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:43.870
One of the last things Sister Lilith says
to Sister Beatrice in the Season 2 finale

00:10:43.870 --> 00:10:46.310
is that a dark future awaits them.

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:47.990
"There's a holy war coming.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:51.892
I really hope we end up on the same side."

00:10:51.892 --> 00:10:53.520
What exactly does this mean?

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:55.769
Hints are planted throughout the entire season.

00:10:55.769 --> 00:10:59.829
The nature of the Other Side, the realm at
the other end of the portal that Dr. Jillian

00:10:59.829 --> 00:11:02.130
Salvius creates, is not exactly clear.

00:11:02.130 --> 00:11:06.139
Its existence is first made known when Adriel
arrives on Earth after ripping open a gateway

00:11:06.139 --> 00:11:08.070
from his world using the Halo.

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:13.401
He's pursued by Tarasks, monstrous demons
whose sole purpose is to regain the mystical object.

00:11:13.401 --> 00:11:17.329
Lilith is dramatically changed by her time
on the Other Side after she's killed, and

00:11:17.329 --> 00:11:19.850
Jillian sends her over again through the gate.

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:23.769
What feels like seconds for Jillian is days
for Lilith, who walks through a desert until

00:11:23.769 --> 00:11:26.990
she's expelled by an entity that does not
want her there.

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:31.080
Miguel wanders the same desert as a boy until
he's rescued by wandering angels and taken

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:32.250
to the shining city.

00:11:32.250 --> 00:11:36.000
He's raised in Reya's court and trained as
a weapon to use against Adriel.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.380
Reya later helps Ava defeat Adriel.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:41.690
Is Reya a god, a demon, an angel, or something
else entirely?

00:11:41.690 --> 00:11:45.751
Is she going to start the holy war against
Earth, or will someone bring the fight to her?

00:11:45.751 --> 00:11:48.538
What are her motivations and intentions regarding
Earth?

00:11:48.538 --> 00:11:52.339
Like many of the most powerful figures on
the show, her motivations are inscrutable

00:11:52.339 --> 00:11:54.430
— and absolutely fascinating.

